---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import HeroPipeline from '../components/marketing/HeroPipeline.astro';
import AgentQuickstart from '../components/marketing/AgentQuickstart.astro';
import ApiDemo from '../components/marketing/ApiDemo.astro';
import Architecture from '../components/marketing/Architecture.astro';
import Dashboard from '../components/marketing/Dashboard.astro';
import Faq from '../components/marketing/Faq.astro';
import Pricing from '../components/Pricing.astro';
import Closing from '../components/Closing.astro';
import '../styles/marketing.css';
const problems = [
 {number:'01',icon:'lock',title:'Blocked requests',text:'Auto mode climbs from plain HTTP to residential IPs and a real browser, and stops at the site’s real answer.'},
 {number:'02',icon:'code',title:'JavaScript pages',text:'Empty JavaScript shells move to a hardened Firefox browser on their own. Ask for render: always to start there.'},
 {number:'03',icon:'globe',title:'Geo-specific content',text:'FetchX uses the exit country that worked for the site before, or the one you set.'},
 {number:'04',icon:'layers',title:'Captchas',text:'Turnstile, reCAPTCHA and hCaptcha are solved in the browser when they appear.'},
 {number:'05',icon:'route',title:'Paying for failures',text:'Only a successful request is charged, at the price of the step that got the data.'},
];
const faqs = [
 ['What is FetchX?', 'FetchX is a Web Scraping API and Web Unblocker for developers, data teams and AI agents. Send a URL; FetchX picks the cheapest route that works, uses a browser and solves captchas when it must, and returns HTML, markdown or a screenshot.'],
 ['Can I send any URL to the API?', 'Any public http or https URL. Private, local and cloud-metadata addresses are refused, checked after DNS and on every redirect.'],
 ['How do HTTP fetching and browser rendering work?', 'One endpoint, POST /v1/fetch, does both. Auto mode tries HTTP first and moves to a browser when the page is an empty JavaScript shell or HTTP is blocked. render: always starts in a browser; render: never stays on HTTP.'],
 ['What happens if a connection drops?', 'Send an idempotency_key with each request. Resending the same body with the same key returns the first result and is never charged twice.'],
 ['Am I charged for failed requests?', 'No. Blocks, timeouts and every earlier failed attempt cost nothing. A failed request returns a clear reason and a next step instead.'],
 ['How do I buy credits?', 'Sign in and open Credits & usage. Choose a credit pack and pay once with Stripe: card in USD or UPI in INR. Purchased credits do not expire.'],
];
---
<Layout title="FetchX — Unlock the web. With one API." description="FetchX brings proxy routing, browser rendering and challenge handling into one API for developers, data teams and AI agents.">
 <div class="mkt">
  <section class="mkt-hero mkt-container">
   <div class="mkt-hero-copy"><p class="mkt-eyebrow"><span class="mkt-dot"></span> WEB SCRAPING API & WEB UNBLOCKER</p><h1>Unlock the web.<br/><span>With one API.</span></h1><p class="mkt-hero-description">FetchX brings proxy routing, browser rendering and challenge handling into one API for developers, data teams and AI agents.</p><div class="mkt-actions"><a class="mkt-button mkt-button-primary" href="/signup">Start building <Icon name="arrow" size={18}/></a><a class="mkt-button mkt-button-secondary" href="/docs">Explore the API <Icon name="code" size={18}/></a></div><a class="mkt-text-link mkt-hero-agent-link" href="#agent-quickstart"><Icon name="code" size={15}/> Quickstart for coding agents <Icon name="down" size={14}/></a></div>
   <div class="mkt-hero-visual"><HeroPipeline/></div>
  </section>
  <div class="mkt-capabilities mkt-container"><span class="mkt-micro">ONE ACCESS LAYER</span><span><Icon name="route" size={16}/> Auto routing</span><span><Icon name="code" size={16}/> Browser rendering</span><span><Icon name="lock" size={16}/> Captcha solving</span><span><Icon name="file" size={16}/> Markdown output</span></div>

  <AgentQuickstart/>

  <section class="mkt-section mkt-container" id="api"><div class="mkt-section-heading"><div><span class="mkt-eyebrow">01 / THE DEVELOPER EXPERIENCE</span><h2>A familiar request.<br/><span class="mkt-muted">A clearer result.</span></h2></div><p>Send a URL. Get the page, in the format you want, with every attempt and what it cost.</p></div><ApiDemo/></section>

  <section class="mkt-problems-section"><div class="mkt-container"><div class="mkt-section-heading"><div><span class="mkt-eyebrow">02 / THE WEB HAS SHARP EDGES</span><h2>Your next feature shouldn’t<br/>be proxy infrastructure.</h2></div><p>Put the access work behind an API, so your application can focus on what the data makes possible.</p></div><div class="mkt-problems">{problems.map(problem=><article><div class="mkt-problem-top"><Icon name={problem.icon} size={23}/><span>{problem.number}</span></div><h3>{problem.title}</h3><p>{problem.text}</p></article>)}</div></div></section>

  <section class="mkt-section mkt-container" id="platform"><div class="mkt-section-heading"><div><span class="mkt-eyebrow">03 / UNDER THE SURFACE</span><h2>One access layer.<br/><span class="mkt-muted">Room for what’s next.</span></h2></div><p>Routes, a browser and captcha solving behind one call, with what worked remembered per site.</p></div><Architecture/></section>

  <section class="mkt-dashboard-section"><div class="mkt-container"><div class="mkt-section-heading"><div><span class="mkt-eyebrow">04 / THE CONTROL ROOM</span><h2>See the request.<br/>Understand the result.</h2></div><div><span class="mkt-tag mkt-tag-preview">CONSOLE DESIGN PREVIEW</span><p>An illustration with synthetic data. Open the console to try a URL in the playground and see every request.</p></div></div><Dashboard/><a class="mkt-text-link mkt-dashboard-demo-link" href="/app">Open workspace <Icon name="arrow" size={16}/></a></div></section>

  <section class="mkt-section mkt-container" id="use-cases"><div class="mkt-section-heading"><div><span class="mkt-eyebrow">05 / BUILT INTO YOUR WORKFLOW</span><h2>The web is a source.<br/><span class="mkt-muted">What will you build?</span></h2></div><a class="mkt-text-link" href="/developers">Build with FetchX <Icon name="arrow" size={17}/></a></div><div class="mkt-use-cases">
   <a class="mkt-use-case" href="/use-cases/ai-agents"><div class="mkt-use-case-art mkt-agent-art" aria-hidden="true"><span class="mkt-art-label">RETRIEVAL / 01</span><div class="mkt-agent-prompt"><Icon name="code" size={18}/><span>Read the source.</span><i></i></div><div class="mkt-agent-result"><span>source.context</span><i></i><i></i><i></i><b><Icon name="check" size={12}/> ready to inspect</b></div></div><div class="mkt-use-case-content"><span class="mkt-micro">AI & AUTOMATION</span><h3>Give your agent<br/>a way into the web.</h3><p>Bring source content into retrieval, research and agent workflows with explicit access controls.</p><span class="mkt-use-case-link">Explore AI agents <Icon name="diagonal" size={18}/></span></div></a>
   <a class="mkt-use-case" href="/use-cases/price-monitoring"><div class="mkt-use-case-art mkt-price-art" aria-hidden="true"><span class="mkt-art-label">MARKET SIGNAL / 02</span><div class="mkt-chart-grid"></div><svg viewBox="0 0 320 130"><path d="M0 95 35 95 35 70 80 70 80 82 120 82 120 47 170 47 170 62 215 62 215 28 270 28 270 40 320 40"/><circle cx="215" cy="28" r="4"/></svg><div class="mkt-price-marker">price.changed <span>↓</span></div></div><div class="mkt-use-case-content"><span class="mkt-micro">COMMERCE & RETAIL</span><h3>Turn price changes<br/>into market signals.</h3><p>Feed your own monitoring pipeline with product pages, availability and source-level evidence.</p><span class="mkt-use-case-link">Explore price monitoring <Icon name="diagonal" size={18}/></span></div></a>
   <a class="mkt-use-case" href="/use-cases/real-estate"><div class="mkt-use-case-art mkt-property-art" aria-hidden="true"><span class="mkt-art-label">PROPERTY DATA / 03</span><div class="mkt-map-grid"></div><span class="mkt-map-pin mkt-map-pin-one"><Icon name="house" size={17}/></span><span class="mkt-map-pin mkt-map-pin-two"><Icon name="house" size={14}/></span><span class="mkt-map-pin mkt-map-pin-three"><Icon name="house" size={14}/></span><div class="mkt-property-label"><span>listing.reference</span><b>Source connected <Icon name="arrow" size={12}/></b></div></div><div class="mkt-use-case-content"><span class="mkt-micro">PROPERTY & RESEARCH</span><h3>Build a clearer view<br/>of the property market.</h3><p>Connect listing and public property sources to your own matching, validation and analysis.</p><span class="mkt-use-case-link">Explore real estate <Icon name="diagonal" size={18}/></span></div></a>
  </div><p class="mkt-small-note">Illustrative workflows. Your application validates the data it receives.</p></section>

  <section class="mkt-pricing-section mkt-container" id="pricing"><div class="mkt-section-heading"><div><span class="mkt-eyebrow">06 / PREPAID FETCHX CREDITS</span><h2>Start with trial credits.<br/><span class="mkt-muted">Top up as you go.</span></h2></div><a class="mkt-text-link" href="/pricing">View pricing <Icon name="arrow" size={17}/></a></div><Pricing compact/></section>

  <section class="mkt-section mkt-container mkt-faq-section"><div><span class="mkt-eyebrow">07 / A FEW MORE DETAILS</span><h2>Good questions.<br/><span class="mkt-muted">Clear answers.</span></h2><p class="mkt-faq-intro">Get to know the API, the access model and where the product is headed.</p><a class="mkt-text-link" href="/docs">Go deeper in the docs <Icon name="arrow" size={16}/></a></div><Faq items={faqs}/></section>
  <Closing/>
 </div>
 <script>import '../scripts/marketing.ts';</script>
</Layout>

<style>
 .mkt-hero-agent-link{gap:8px;margin-top:14px;min-height:36px}
 .mkt-hero-agent-link:hover svg:last-child{transform:translateY(3px)}
</style>
